 "conclusion": "HYPOTHESIS REFUTED, and the refutation is informative. Suppressing the lattice does not expose the aperiodic signal, it destroys registration outright: above-pitch bands collapse to 12.5%, 7.5%, 0.0%, 0.0%, 0.0%. The lattice is what allows the correlation to lock onto a position at all -- it cannot say WHICH period is correct, but without it there is nothing to register against, because the aperiodic residual alone is too weak. This is the same wall dense_residual_ceiling.json hit, reached from a third direction. The shipped (2.0, 8.0) is the best config in the grid: tied on <=1 px with (1.0,4.0) and (1.5,6.0) at 37.5% but strictly better on tiered credit (16.6 vs 15.0 pts/40). The default was accidentally near-optimal and no change is warranted.",
 "caveats": [
  "n=40, so the 37.5% point estimate is noisy (the authoritative shipped figure is 29.6% at n=280); the conclusion rests on the ordering and on the collapse of the above-pitch arms, both of which are far larger than sampling noise.",
  "Grid is 12 points, not exhaustive; a finer search near (2,8) was not run because the three best configs are already statistically indistinguishable on <=1 px.",
  "p2_val only; no organizer data used."
 ],
